# Deferred images

**Never show an image (or UI that depends on it) before the bitmap is ready.** Skeleton until load (or initials/fallback). This is app-wide.

## Rules

1. Do not use a bare `<img>` in feature UI. Use `DeferredImage` or `AppAvatar`.
2. `DeferredImage` — remote/local bitmaps (logos, QR, product art). Skeleton in place until `onLoad`; handle cache via `img.complete`.
3. `AppAvatar` — app favicons. Skeleton until favicon loads or initials fallback; expose `onReady`.
4. List/detail rows that include an avatar must keep the **whole row/card** on a skeleton (or `media-preload` under the skeleton) until `onReady`. Do not flash name/spent/amount beside an empty icon.
5. Prefer keeping the image mounted under `.media-preload` while the skeleton shows — do not `display:none` / unmount the loader in a way that blocks network load, then remount a second avatar after ready (that re-flashes a skeleton).
6. Permission dialogs and detail panels follow the same gate when they show an app icon.

## Imports

- `DeferredImage` from `src/components/DeferredImage.tsx`
- `AppAvatar` from `src/components/AppAvatar.tsx`
- Skeleton primitives from `src/components/Skeleton.tsx`
